   {
    "text": "<<The Ode to the Second Amendment>>  \n\nO, what a marvel is this! Why doth the 2nd Amendment, once a flame of liberty, now seem but ash and dust?  \n\nAh, ye who ponder this, let us not forget the spirit of the law, that right and justice doth dwell in every hand.  \n\nThe right to bear arms, once a shield against tyranny, now is deemed obsolete, as if the sword of justice hath been replaced by the sword of peace.  \n\nBut mark ye, friend, that the heart of man doth not lie in the gun, but in the will to defend what is dear.  \n\nThe 2nd Amendment is not a relic, but a rallying cry, a testament to the enduring spirit of freedom.  \n\nSo let us not cast it aside, but let it be a beacon, guiding us through the shadows of doubt.  \n\nFor in the end, it is not the gun that matters, but the soul that holds it.",
